Applied to this claim, single-purchase gift buyers rather than replenishment shoppers illustrate behavioural, not demographic segmentation. That is why the sentence does not survive careful reading.

Students often remember that two concepts differ but swap the direction of the comparison. Verify which side of the pair is longer, larger, riskier, or more regulated.

Because the decisive detail is wrong, mark the statement false.', 'FALSE — This statement is false. A segment of a northern province and southern retail catchment is automatically profitable whenever it can be named on a map.

